    "body": "> I thought that using strictly split meant to throw everything after the second colon away because of this discussion: https://github.com/whatwg/dom/issues/1387#issuecomment-3029579206\r\n\r\nDunno — but the PR which resulted in the local-name-computation part of the spec ending up as it is now, https://github.com/whatwg/dom/pull/1135, is from 2022. So it predates that https://github.com/whatwg/dom/issues/1387#issuecomment-3029579206 discussion (~8 months ago) by more than 2 years. The only actual spec change made in response to that https://github.com/whatwg/dom/issues/1387#issuecomment-3029579206 discussion was https://github.com/whatwg/dom/pull/1388/changes — which was, **“If _prefix_ is not a _valid namespace prefix_, then throw”** (no new effect on the requirements about the local name).",
